 ```
 
+### Windows PowerShell
+
+Run from the repository root. No virtual environment activation or execution
+policy change is needed:
+
+```powershell
+npm.cmd ci
+python -m venv tools/flash/.venv
+.\tools\flash\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r tools/flash/requirements.txt
+```
+
+Verify the installation without connecting an arm:
+
+```powershell
+npm.cmd test
+.\tools\flash\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m unittest discover -s tools/flash/tests
+npm.cmd run settings -- --help
+.\tools\flash\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tools/flash/flash.py --help
+```
+
+When the adapter is connected, set `$env:SERVO_PORT = 'COM3'` with its actual
+port. Use `npm.cmd` instead of `npm` in the commands below, and use
+`.\tools\flash\.venv\Scripts\python.exe` instead of the Unix environment path.
+Hardware discovery, backups, calibration and flashing require the powered motor
+bus. The optional telemetry viewer has its own installation in
+[tools/simulation/README.md](tools/simulation/README.md).
+
 Replace the port with yours, such as `/dev/ttyUSB0` on Linux. Examples use motor
 ID **1** and baud **1000000**; adjust these to match your servo.
 
